  "question": {
    "text": "If the rate of increase of the radius of a circle is $5 \\mathrm{~cm} / \\mathrm{sec}$, then the rate of increase of its area, when the radius is $20 \\mathrm{~cm}$, will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$10 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$20 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$200 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$400 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $\\mathrm{A}=\\pi \\mathrm{r}^2 \\quad \\frac{d r}{d t}=5$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{dA}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=2 \\pi r \\frac{\\mathrm{dr}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=2 \\pi 20(5) \\\\\n& =200 \\pi\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}